 {"id":"AUG-121","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Model each Auger task as a scoped XML spec with explicit in/out references and ch:trace links","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: a task is itself a small spec for one exact request, or it names the exact reusable spec blocks in scope and the relevant blocks explicitly out of scope. It must be searchable in one pass and preserve active/inactive, levels, verification, and provenance. Scope for THIS row: XML task element schema; stable task id matching the canonical board id; explicit in_scope refs, out_of_scope refs plus exclusion reason, acceptance/verification refs, status/version; approved-plan export using only supported boardctl fields; ch:trace spec IDs. Exclusions: do not change GitReins, scheduler dispatch, boardctl storage schema, or existing tasks 118/119/120; no direct JSONL writer, no LLM inference, no automatic task approval. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#requirements (R2,R3,R4,R9,R10) and #acceptance-criteria (AC-6,AC-7,AC-9,AC-15).\nch:trace row=AUG-121 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#requirements wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/prd/xml-spec-graph-2026-10-29","acceptance_criteria":"1. Given a task XML block, when validation runs, then its stable ID, lifecycle/version, in-scope refs, out-of-scope refs with reasons, acceptance refs, and verification methods are typed and resolve to existing blocks; proof: tests/test_xml_task_contract.py::test_task_scope_contract.\n2. Given duplicate, missing, inactive-without-acknowledgment, or cross-version spec references, when validation runs, then it returns a typed finding naming the exact task and block IDs without emitting a partial task packet; proof: the negative fixture cases in tests/test_xml_task_contract.py.\n3.