 {"id":"AUG-122","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Resolve a task or code location to a minimal XML spec context bundle in one query","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: when an agent reaches code it does not understand, it must use the same graph/query tool to find the spec related to that code instantly; one search returns only relevant blocks, not the irrelevant corpus. Scope for THIS row: a read-only Auger context query keyed by task ID, XML block ID/ch:trace spec reference, code path, or symbol; deterministic relationship expansion; include task scope and exclusion summary; report active/inactive state and verification. Exclusions: no full-corpus fallback, no code/spec edits, no arbitrary remote URL fetch, no second semantic/LLM backend, no GitReins hook wiring (GR-154). Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly, #relationship-and-verification-graph, and #acceptance-criteria (AC-3,AC-4,AC-8,AC-9,AC-14).\nch:trace row=AUG-122 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#selection-and-assembly wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/prd/xml-spec-graph-2026-10-29","acceptance_criteria":"1. Given an Auger task ID, when the context query runs once, then it returns that task block, only its in-scope requirements/acceptance/verification blocks, and a compact explicit out-of-scope list with exclusion reasons; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_task_context_excludes_unrelated_blocks.\n2. Given a source path or symbol with a ch:trace spec reference, when the context query runs, then it resolves the exact XML block and declared graph closure with source file, ID, version, active status, applicability, verification method, and relationship edge; proof: tests/test_spec_context.py::test_code_trace_context.\n3. Given no trace, an unkno