 {"id": "QA-AUGER-16", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "title": "[P2] bunker-mvp cannot spawn agents — logind enable-linger hangs, blocking every clean-machine battery", "reasoning": "Verified live 2026-10-30T19:36Z-19:44Z during the QA-AUGER-15 re-verification. bunker-mvp (bunkerd 0.2.1, ONLINE, Disk 115.2 GiB free / 20% used, Agents 0/50) cannot create an agent: every spawn dies at stage rootless-install because 'enable linger' hangs. journalctl -u bunkerd shows three consecutive attempts on 2026-10-30 between 19:38:35Z and 19:43:47Z (agent ids 25c271dd, 2f800c24, 35cc666e), each ending: 'spawn <id> failed at stage rootless-install: install rootless docker for bunker-<id>: enable linger for bunker-<id>: exit status 1 (output: Could not enable linger: Connection timed out; linger marker /var/lib/systemd/linger/bunker-<id> absent; linger enable attempts: 3)', followed by rollback (loginctl disable-linger, userdel) and NO surviving agent. A bare probe reproduces the host fault with no auger or battery involved: 'timeout 15 loginctl enable-linger <user>' on the host hangs and never returns, while systemd-logind reports active with NRestarts=0 and /var/lib/systemd/linger holds only root. This is a logind/dbus fault, NOT disk (115 GiB free) and NOT the auger product. Two further defects observed in the same evidence: (a) the harness's bunker-qa.sh appended a CONTRADICTORY classification to its spawn-failure row - '[root cause: agent ssh port 22 AND port 22 unreachable on bunker-mvp - server/network down, not a docker fault]' - even though ssh to the host was reachable throughout the window and the failure happens DURING spawn, before any agent ssh endpoint exists, so a future reader is pointed at the network instead of at logind; (b) repeated failed spawns mutate host residue (orphan user/home/key counts changed across the window: 2 orphan users/2 orphan homes -> 1/1) because the rollback is best-effort. Impact: the QA lane cannot admit ANY clea